A||||8||Ken Wittlief||84 sport coupe w/30k - a good project car?!||||5||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||04-18-2001||11:22 PM||||found an '84:<P>less than 30k original miles<BR>2.5L w/auto<BR>interior looks great, grey fabric, no rips, clean<P>The car has been left out in the sun alot and the paint is terrible, the roof looks and feels like it has been sandblasted, and the formerly black hood looks ashen grey.<BR>battery is dead<BR>needs tires<BR>master cylinder and some brake lines replaced, but not bled correctly<BR>kid says he blew the head gasket, and after replacing it the engine 'sputters' (havent hear it run yet)<BR>has a new windshield<P>the owner wants $400, and I would have to tow it home since its not running right.<P>Does this sound like a good project car? The low miles on the drive train, and the nice interior is tempting<P>but I dont know what the kid did to the engine when he replaced the head gasket (cracked a manifold maybe?!) and the paint is really bad, might be better off replacing the roof and hood than trying to get them paintable again.<P>Think this car could be put back in reasonable condition for less than $1k?<P>Isnt 30k miles about the point where the front end starts needing new everything on an 84?<P>whats the general consensus? go for it or hold out for an '88?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-19-2001||12:20 AM||||Hey Ken!<BR>Depending on what you want to spend in restoring it, it sounds good...<BR>I would toss the engine, as the kid probly over reved the engine, and neglected oil changes/adds...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||04-19-2001||12:23 AM||||for the price of a motor and paint, you could buy one in much better condition.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||04-19-2001||12:28 AM||||that is one thing I was wondering, what would one have to do to a 2.5 to blow the head gasket?!<P>how can you over-rev an auto, unless he was power shifting it?!||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||04-19-2001||12:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>how can you over-rev an auto, unless he was power shifting it?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've done that a few times, but the RPMs never drop fast enough to get any power when I stomp on it again, I rev it up to about 4k in 1st, then switch to 2nd, and the RPMs don't drop right away.. I have to let off the throttle and wait for them to drop down. if I'd just floored it in 2nd or 3rd, it wouldn't have done that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>so I think I'll just keep it in 3rd.. replace the tranny fluid and get a shift kit.. cause I don't like the engine making funny noises at me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>As for the project car... it could be a good deal depending on what you want to do with it.. if you wanted to turn it into a convertible with a 3.1 V6 in it.. then sure, it's good. if you want to restore it to mint.. then you'd be better off finding one with a better body maybe.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000005||My7Fieros||04-19-2001||02:06 AM||||Go for it! Head gasket is cheap and relativly easy repair (on a 4 banger)...paint is no big deal either. Under 30k miles? Id fix it! Itd be a shame to let it go w/soooooooooo little miles..especially for so cheap! Buy it and fix it up! M7F||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||04-19-2001||09:28 AM||||Well.... Im gonna pass on this one. The idea of coolant getting into the crankcase gives me the willies, I dont know how long the kid drove it with the head gasket blown, esp since the car is not running right with the new head gasket.<P>And since he managed to blow the head gasket in the first place I dont feel too confident about the condition of the auto tranny either.<P>If anyone else is interested in this car let me know and I will send the owners email address to you. The car is located near Geneseo, NY.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spektyr||04-19-2001||12:21 PM||||Number one rule of restoring cars.<P>Buy the best car you can.  Worry about the resto money afterwards.<P>If someone can blow the head gasket in 30k miles one of 2 things is true.<P>1.  The odometer actually should read 130k miles.<BR>2.  Some retard was either powershifting, or running the car in Low with their foot on the floor.  (Did that in a junker chevy once.  Gaskets held but it burned a quart of oil in 5 seconds.)||||reg||1
Z||000008||deceler8||04-19-2001||04:40 PM||||Get him down to $200 and go for it.<P>You can just paint whatever panels need it and get a used engine.<P>Or get it and part it.||||reg||1
